| Provider webhook | Submit signed provider event to one provider endpoint. | Raw-body signature and replay validation precede parse; no general API session. |"}],"amendments":["Rewrite AC-INF-01's mandatory sequence for the declared anonymous-browser principal. After boundary validation, classify the request against the registered public auth class and allowlisted cache class, authorize only the registered public projection, state that human session and acting-context resolution are not applicable, and state that `If-Match` and `Idempotency-Key` are neither required nor accepted as authority. Preserve the existing safe-cache/forwarding behavior, typed non-disclosing refusal, HTTP 200 response contract, and no-audit/no-idempotency/no-outbox persistence rule.","Rewrite AC-INF-09's mandatory sequence for the declared provider-webhook principal. Verify raw-body signature, replay window, and provider/endpoint binding before parsing; authorize only that endpoint's registered provider scope; derive receipt identity from `(provider, external_event_id)`; and state that no human session, acting party, `If-Match`, or business-command idempotency key is applicable. Preserve rapid acknowledgement, asynchronous durable processing, signature-oracle resistance, and exactly-one `WebhookReceipt` deduplication semantics.","Do not introduce one generic replacement phrase for every machine flow. Keep the wording explicitly principal-polymorphic so AC-INF-01 names anonymous-route/projection authority and AC-INF-09 names provider signature/endpoint/receipt authority. These are G00's two members of FLOW-001's 29-criterion population."],"acceptanceChecks":["AC-INF-01 contains no mandatory human authentication or acting-context-resolution step and no revision/idempotency enforcement step; its ordered sequence names registered public-route classification and public-projection authorization instead.","AC-INF-09 contains no mandatory human authentication or acting-context-resolution step; raw-body signature, replay-window, and provider-endpoint binding precede parse, and receipt deduplication remains `(provider, external_event_id)`.","A deterministic scan of AC-INF-01 and AC-INF-09 finds no criterion that both declares no session/acting context and mandates `authenticate and resolve acting context`.","Existing success, failure, latency, caching, audit, receipt, and recovery outcomes in the two criteria remain present and testable; amendment changes authority stages only.","Independent whole-population verification re-runs FLOW-001's exact 29 acceptance-criterion IDs after all range groups apply their owned amendments."],"classification":"mechanical"},{"id":"G00-W02","findingIds":["IA-IDX-F-001"],"writablePaths":["/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/index.md"],"sourceCitations":[{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/index.md","lineStart":9,"lineEnd":9,"quote":"Read 00-infrastructure first, then feature shards in numerical dependency order. Dependencies only point to lower-numbered shards."},{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/14-services-marketplace.md","lineStart":741,"lineEnd":741,"quote":"[Shard 18 § Calculation, Statement and Financial Gate](18-royalty-accounting.md#calculation-statement-and-financial-gate)"},{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/15-education-delivery.md","lineStart":663,"lineEnd":663,"quote":"[Shard 17 § Contracts](17-realtime-sessions.md#contracts) and [Shard 17 § Event Schemas](17-realtime-sessions.md#event-schemas)"},{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/15-education-delivery.md","lineStart":663,"lineEnd":663,"quote":"[Shard 41 § Contracts](41-career-finance.md#contracts)"},{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/decomposition-plan.md","lineStart":60,"lineEnd":61,"quote":"| 14 | 14-services-marketplace.md | Services marketplace lifecycle | 05.01–05.07 | 7 | High | Feature domain | Yes | 00, 01, 06, 09, 10 |
| 15 | 15-education-delivery.md | Lessons, practice and mentorship delivery | 06.01–06.03, 06.05–06.07 | 6 | High | Feature domain | Yes | 00, 01, 02, 06 |"}],"amendments":["Replace the false blanket lower-number rule in `## Reading Order` with an explicit two-class graph contract: read Shard 00 first; use the approved decomposition plan's dependency column as the build-order prerequisite DAG; treat anchored runtime integrations and inbound-only reciprocal-consumer links in shard rosters as non-ordering edges unless the same edge is also present in the plan's prerequisite column.","State that numerical shard number is an identifier, not by itself a dependency proof. A higher-numbered anchored integration can be consumed by a lower-numbered shard without changing build order when the lower shard's contract defines a boundary against the later-owned capability and the decomposition plan does not list it as a prerequisite.","Limit this work item to the owned index wording. Other range owners must reconcile Shards 14 and 15 and the decomposition-plan rows under the same IA-IDX-F-001 ID; G00 must not delete or reclassify their source edges without those owners' source review."],"acceptanceChecks":["`index.md` no longer says all dependencies point to lower-numbered shards.","Reading order names one mechanically testable source for build prerequisites: the decomposition plan's dependency column.","Index text distinguishes build-order prerequisite, runtime integration, and inbound-only reciprocal-consumer edge semantics and explains when a higher-numbered link affects ordering.","After all range amendments, a graph check finds no roster edge classified as a build prerequisite that is absent from the decomposition plan and no plan prerequisite absent from its shard roster; non-ordering integrations are excluded from topological sorting."],"classification":"structural"},{"id":"G00-W03","findingIds":["IA-IDX-F-002"],"writablePaths":["/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/index.md"],"sourceCitations":[{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/index.md","lineStart":62,"lineEnd":62,"quote":"- Cross-shard dependencies are bidirectional in skeleton metadata and directional in the approved plan."},{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/07-credits-core.md","lineStart":686,"lineEnd":686,"quote":"[Shard 01](01-identity-authority.md)"},{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/12-community-spaces-events.md","lineStart":488,"lineEnd":488,"quote":"[Shard 06](06-trust-safety.md)"},{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/06-trust-safety.md","lineStart":1063,"lineEnd":1063,"quote":"[Shard 12 — Community spaces and events Contracts](12-community-spaces-events.md#contracts)"},{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/15-education-delivery.md","lineStart":663,"lineEnd":663,"quote":"[Shard 06](06-trust-safety.md)"}],"amendments":["Extend `## Conventions` with a normative cross-shard citation contract: every source-side edge must name its direction (`consume`, `publish`, `call`, `subscribe`, or `inbound only`), the concrete boundary consumed or produced, and an exact destination heading anchor. A file-only shard link is invalid.","Require reciprocal metadata to agree on producer, consumer, canonical owner, concrete contract/event/command/model identifier, and typed failure/unknown-state behavior without copying the destination's owned contract prose.","Keep amendment at index policy level. The 30 file-only references in Shards 07 through 15 remain owned by their respective range groups under the same IA-IDX-F-002 ID."],"acceptanceChecks":["`index.md` explicitly rejects file-only cross-shard references and requires exact heading anchors plus named boundary semantics.","A deterministic scan of the authoritative 30-edge population returns zero file-only source references after all range groups apply their amendments.","Every amended edge's anchor resolves to an existing destination heading, and source/target descriptions agree on direction and canonical ownership.","No source amendment copies a destination's full contract; it cites the owned destination section and names only the consumed boundary."],"classification":"mechanical"},{"id":"G00-W04","findingIds":["CON-003"],"writablePaths":["/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/00-infrastructure.md"],"sourceCitations":[{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/00-infrastructure.md","lineStart":404,"lineEnd":404,"quote":"- **Shard 01 — Identity authority and party governance:** consume [Shard 01 — Identity authority and party governance Contracts](01-identity-authority.md#contracts) into this shard `§ Contracts`; publish this shard `§ Event Schemas` to [Shard 01 — Identity authority and party governance Event Schemas](01-identity-authority.md#event-schemas). Canonical ownership stays with the producer and typed failure/unknown states cross the same boundary."},{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/00-infrastructure.md","lineStart":94,"lineEnd":96,"quote":"| `userId` | UUID/null | Verified Supabase Auth subject; never accepted from request data. |
| `actingPartyId` | UUID/null | Resolved server-side from eligible memberships/mandates. |
| `capabilities` | readonly string[] | Server-derived and resource-scoped; never trusted from JWT user metadata. |"},{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/01-identity-authority.md","lineStart":91,"lineEnd":95,"quote":"| Canonical party | `person|alias|organization`, PostgreSQL UUID, immutable kind, explicit lifecycle/version. An alias is a party but never signs; a person/legal entity signs. |
| Facet vocabulary | Versioned platform registry initially containing `performer, writer, producer, engineer, teacher, seller, tech`; no primary facet; petitions enter a curation queue and never create live values directly. |
| Alias ownership | Exactly one owner at a time through non-overlapping dated periods. Display names are non-unique; public handles are globally unique after Unicode/confusable normalization and never reissued. |
| Legal identity | Protected fields are stored/read separately from public projections, never browser-cached, and disclosed only by purpose/audience allowlist. |
| Acting context | Derived, not configured. Stable order: up to five pins → self → aliases by creation → organizations/represented parties alphabetically; frozen while open; filter at eight contexts. |"},{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/00-infrastructure.md","lineStart":293,"lineEnd":306,"quote":"```ts
type PlatformEvent<T extends JsonValue> = {
  eventId: string;
  eventType: string;
  schemaVersion: number;
  occurredAt: string;
  aggregateType: string;
  aggregateId: string;
  aggregateVersion: number;
  correlationId: string;
  causationId: string | null;
  actorId: string | null;
  actingPartyId: string | null;
  payload: T;"},{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/01-identity-authority.md","lineStart":577,"lineEnd":583,"quote":"All events use Shard 00's `PlatformEvent`; payloads contain identifiers only.

| Event type | Payload | Consumer contract |
|---|---|---|
| `identity.facet.changed.v1` | `{ personId, facetCode }` | Navigation/search refetch person version. |
| `identity.alias.changed.v1` | `{ aliasId }` | Public profile, credits, redirects refetch canonical alias. |
| `identity.acting-context.revoked.v1` | `{ personId, partyId, relationshipId }` | Session/UI purges cached context; commands already revalidate. |"}],"amendments":["Replace Shard 00's generic bilateral Shard 01 contract-map sentence with source-derived semantics. State that Shard 00 consumes Shard 01's canonical-party and `Acting context` rules plus membership, representation, mandate, and capability resolution to derive `RequestContext.userId`, `actingPartyId`, and resource-scoped `capabilities` and to revalidate protected-command authority server-side.","State the reverse platform boundary concretely: Shard 01's identifier-only identity events use Shard 00's `PlatformEvent<T>` envelope, including correlation/causation, aggregate version, nullable actor, and nullable acting-party fields; Shard 00 owns the envelope while Shard 01 owns identity payload/event meaning. Cite the existing `#contracts` and `#event-schemas` anchors; do not duplicate either section's full schema.","Retain typed failure/unknown-state propagation, but bind it to the named authority-resolution and event-envelope boundaries rather than leaving it as a generic whole-section template."],"acceptanceChecks":["The owned Shard 00→01 map entry names `RequestContext.userId`, `actingPartyId`, `capabilities`, canonical party, `Acting context`, membership/representation/mandate/capability resolution, and `PlatformEvent<T>`.","The entry explicitly assigns canonical identity/authority ownership to Shard 01 and platform request/event-envelope ownership to Shard 00.","Both destination anchors resolve, and the amendment agrees with Shard 01's reciprocal line and its statement that all identity events use `PlatformEvent`.","The amended G00 side no longer matches the exact generic whole-section template and contains concrete backticked identifiers sufficient for the persisted semantic-specificity classifier.","Independent CON-003 verification uses a persisted, machine-reproducible classifier over all 268 reciprocal pairs; G00 claims only its owned pair amendment and does not invent a new global count."],"classification":"source-derived"}],"unresolvedDecisions":[],"notes":["Verified immutable inputs exactly: summary.json SHA-256 c36a9ccff2bba37d4f7065e242e7e484d762e65d164fa6ffbcb894c487a83c52; ia-ambiguity-report.md SHA-256 a91d5de055697e3e82f437b1ffefa60ede632997c1619381a99067978bd9e53b; archive-manifest.md SHA-256 883376a1e67a61a946fbb62b4881035ee1f282b1a3eb03f401ba7257cba46e92.","Authoritative population read only from `prioritizedDeduplicatedFindings`; count 87. No superseded 85-finding snapshot used.","G00 writable IA population is exactly `/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/index.md` and `/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/00-infrastructure.md`.","EDGE-SEC-002 is explicit corroboration of INF-VF1 and shares G00-W01 rather than creating a conflicting second amendment.","EDGE-SEC-005 was inspected because it cites Shard 00's principal matrix. No G00 amendment is warranted: Shard 00 already declares queue/schedule and provider-webhook principal boundaries; required bindings belong to `/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/22-release-distribution.md` under its owning range.","EDGE-SEC-004, SPC-F1, and DD18-XSHARD-01 mention or consume Shard 00 but require no edits in G00-owned paths; their amendments belong to Shard 23, Shard 12, and deep dive 18 respectively.","CON-003's persisted classifier and 268-pair global recount are orchestration/verification obligations outside this exclusive IA path range. G00-W04 supplies only the source-backed amendment for G00's owned reciprocal pair.","No genuine product or architecture decision remains after destination inspection; all G00 amendments are mechanical, structural, or source-derived."]},{"groupId":"G01","inputHashesChecked":true,"findingIds":["CON-003","CON-001","FLOW-001","PRF-VF1","MAT-001"],"workItems":[{"id":"G01-CON-003-SEMANTIC-CONTRACTS","findingIds":["CON-003"],"writablePaths":["/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/01-identity-authority.md","/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/02-profiles-verification.md","/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/03-cms-content-modeling.md","/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/04-cms-delivery-media.md","/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/05-platform-configuration-admin.md"],"sourceCitations":[{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/01-identity-authority.md","lineStart":666,"lineEnd":666,"quote":"- **Shard 02 — Profiles, claiming and qualifications:** consume [Shard 02 — Profiles, claiming and qualifications Contracts](02-profiles-verification.md#contracts) into this shard `§ Contracts`; publish this shard `§ Event Schemas` to [Shard 02 — Profiles, claiming and qualifications Event Schemas](02-profiles-verification.md#event-schemas). Canonical ownership stays with the producer and typed failure/unknown states cross the same boundary."},{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/02-profiles-verification.md","lineStart":560,"lineEnd":560,"quote":"- **Shard 01 — Identity authority and party governance:** consume [Shard 01 — Identity authority and party governance Contracts](01-identity-authority.md#contracts) into this shard `§ Contracts`; publish this shard `§ Event Schemas` to [Shard 01 — Identity authority and party governance Event Schemas](01-identity-authority.md#event-schemas). Canonical ownership stays with the producer and typed failure/unknown states cross the same boundary."},{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/03-cms-content-modeling.md","lineStart":681,"lineEnd":681,"quote":"- **Shard 04 — CMS navigation, media and delivery:** consume [Shard 04 — CMS navigation, media and delivery Contracts](04-cms-delivery-media.md#contracts) into this shard `§ Contracts`; publish this shard `§ Event Schemas` to [Shard 04 — CMS navigation, media and delivery Event Schemas](04-cms-delivery-media.md#event-schemas). Canonical ownership stays with the producer and typed failure/unknown states cross the same boundary."},{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/04-cms-delivery-media.md","lineStart":588,"lineEnd":588,"quote":"- **Shard 03 — CMS content modeling and authoring:** consume [Shard 03 — CMS content modeling and authoring Contracts](03-cms-content-modeling.md#contracts) into this shard `§ Contracts`; publish this shard `§ Event Schemas` to [Shard 03 — CMS content modeling and authoring Event Schemas](03-cms-content-modeling.md#event-schemas). Canonical ownership stays with the producer and typed failure/unknown states cross the same boundary."},{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/05-platform-configuration-admin.md","lineStart":707,"lineEnd":707,"quote":"- **Shard 04 — CMS navigation, media and delivery:** consume [Shard 04 — CMS navigation, media and delivery Contracts](04-cms-delivery-media.md#contracts) into this shard `§ Contracts`; publish this shard `§ Event Schemas` to [Shard 04 — CMS navigation, media and delivery Event Schemas](04-cms-delivery-media.md#event-schemas). Canonical ownership stays with the producer and typed failure/unknown states cross the same boundary."}],"amendments":["Apply the persisted semantic-specificity classifier from the global CON-003 remediation to every reciprocal contract-map edge owned by shards 01-05, not only the four audit examples. For each generic edge, inspect both owning shards' Contracts, Event Schemas, flows, decomposition boundary, ideation source, and delegated deep dive; then replace whole-section dependency prose with concrete command/event/entity identifiers, producer/consumer direction, canonical ownership, and exact target-section links only where those sources establish them.","At minimum, resolve the bilateral Shard 01↔02 and Shard 03↔04 examples cited by the audit. Also review every exact generic bullet in the five owned maps, including shard 05 edges; do not infer a transfer merely because two whole sections are linked. If review proves no concrete transfer, state no dependency/consumption rather than padding identifiers.","Preserve finding ID CON-003 for amendments in this range. The global classifier definition/count record belongs to the global coordinator, not these owned shard files."],"acceptanceChecks":["Every contract-map bullet in shards 01-05 passes the persisted semantic-specificity classifier or explicitly states a source-proven no-consumption boundary.","Shard 01↔02 and Shard 03↔04 maps name the same transfers in reciprocal producer/consumer directions and link exact existing headings.","No bullet introduces a command, event, entity, or ownership rule absent from cited source.","Global rerun inspects all 268 reciprocal pairs and reports at least the reproducible exact-template baseline of 11 bilateral and 69 at-least-one-sided pairs before amendment, then zero unresolved owned G01 pairs after amendment."],"classification":"source-derived"},{"id":"G01-CON-001-TARGET-LINKS","findingIds":["CON-001","PRF-VF1"],"writablePaths":["/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/02-profiles-verification.md","/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/04-cms-delivery-media.md"],"sourceCitations":[{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/02-profiles-verification.md","lineStart":563,"lineEnd":563,"quote":"- **Shard 06 — Trust, safety, disputes and evidence:** inbound only, per DEC-098 — this shard declares no dependency on Shard 06, consumes no Shard 06 contract and cites no Shard 06 section. This shard publishes `profile.contest.changed.v1` from its [§ Event Schemas](#event-schemas), which Shard 06 consumes to open or update the `CaseKind = ownership` case (TSE-01 intake), and exposes a protected inbound command `RecordOwnershipCaseOutcome` in its [§ Contracts](#contracts) — carrying Shard 06's own `case_id`, the contest reference, the TSE-13 outcome, an expected version and an idempotency key — which Shard 06 calls on resolution. This shard applies the profile-control consequence (uphold, transfer or unfreeze) and never adjudicates; canonical case ownership stays with Shard 06, which cannot itself write ownership records, and typed refusal/unknown states cross the same boundary."},{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/06-trust-safety.md","lineStart":1054,"lineEnd":1054,"quote":"- **Shard 02 — Profiles, claiming and qualifications:** command edge only, per DEC-098 — this shard declares no dependency on Shard 02, consumes no Shard 02 contract and reads no Shard 02 store. This shard consumes Shard 02's `profile.contest.changed.v1` only through TSE-01's protected system-signal intake to open or update the `CaseKind = ownership` case, and on TSE-13 final resolution this shard calls Shard 02's protected `RecordOwnershipCaseOutcome` command with this shard's own `case_id`, the contested profile/claim reference, the outcome, the expected Shard 02 aggregate version and an idempotency key. This shard owns case intake, evidence, adjudication and appeal state; Shard 02 alone applies the profile-control consequence and emits its completion event, and typed failure/unknown states cross the same boundary."},{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/04-cms-delivery-media.md","lineStart":590,"lineEnd":590,"quote":"- **Shard 06 — Trust, safety, disputes and evidence:** Shard 06 consumes this shard's [§ Contracts](#contracts) inbound delivery commands `ApplyDeliveryHold` / `ReleaseDeliveryHold` / `RevokeDeliveryEligibility` and this shard's [§ Event Schemas](#event-schemas) for completion evidence. This shard consumes nothing from Shard 06 and cites no Shard 06 section. Canonical adjudication ownership stays with Shard 06; this shard owns only the delivery consequence and its typed refusal/unknown states."},{"path":"/home/rob/Projects/WeJammin/.memory/wiki/specs/ia/06-trust-safety.md","lineStart":1056,"lineEnd":1056,"quote":